{"name":"Grass Blade","hex":"#636f46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grass","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any plant of the family Poaceae, characterized by leaves that arise from nodes in the stem and leaf bases that wrap around the stem, especially those grown as ground cover rather than for grain.","Any of the various plants that are not in the family Poaceae that resemble grasses."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To lay out on the grass; to knock down (an opponent etc.).","To act as a grass or informer, to betray; to report on (criminals etc) to the authorities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grass"},{"term":"blade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The (typically sharp-edged) part of a knife, sword, razor, or other tool with which it cuts.\n\n A sword or knife.\n\nEllipsis of razor blade.","A sword or knife."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To skate on rollerblades.","To furnish with a blade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blade"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poaceae","blocks":[{"text":"Poaceae, also called Gramineae, is a large and nearly ubiquitous family of monocotyledonous flowering plants commonly known as true grasses. It includes the cereal grasses, bamboos, the grasses of natural grassland and species cultivated in lawns and pasture. Poaceae is the most well-known family within the informal group known as grass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Meadow_Foxtail_head.jpg/330px-Meadow_Foxtail_head.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poaceae","wikidata":"Q43238"},{"title":"Grass","blocks":[{"text":"Grass refers to various families of plants. The three major families of grasslike plants are true grasses (Poaceae), sedges (Cyperaceae), and rushes (Juncaceae). Lawns and pasturelands are typically composed of true grasses, five of which cover 46% of the world's arable land: rice, wheat, maize, barley, and sugar cane."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Poa_annua.jpg/330px-Poa_annua.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grass","wikidata":"Q643352"},{"title":"Blade","blocks":[{"text":"A blade is the sharp, cutting portion of a tool, weapon, or machine, specifically designed to puncture, chop, slice, or scrape surfaces or materials. Blades are typically made from materials that are harder than those they are intended to cut. This includes early examples made from flaked stones like flint or obsidian, evolving through the ages into metal forms like copper, bronze, and iron, and culminating in modern versions made from steel or ceramics. Serving as one of humanity's oldest tools, blades continue to have wide-ranging applications, including in combat, cooking, and various other everyday and specialized tasks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Kinmichi_II_-_Short_Sword_with_Black_Lacquer_Saya_-_Walters_511261.jpg/330px-Kinmichi_II_-_Short_Sword_with_Black_Lacquer_Saya_-_Walters_511261.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blade","wikidata":"Q330946"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Grassflowers.jpg/500px-Grassflowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Grassflowers.jpg/1280px-Grassflowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Grassflowers.jpg/500px-Grassflowers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grass flowers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrassflowers.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e